Root cause:
The bug was caused by an invalid memory access that occurred when freeing a link associated with a network in the `link_free` function. Specifically, if a link was attached to a network that utilized bonding, the previous implementation failed to properly remove the link from the bond slaves hashmap before attempting to access and free other resources. This could lead to dereferencing null or already freed pointers, resulting in undefined behavior, memory corruption, or crashes. The patch corrects this by ensuring the proper check and removal of the link from the bond slaves hashmap, thereby preventing the invalid memory access.
